<section class="section" id="mechanics">
  <div class="container two-col">
    <div class="reveal">
      <span class="eyebrow">The insurance mechanics</span>
      <h2>Who actually backs the bond.</h2><div class="divider"></div>
      <p>Surety bail runs on the same principle as any insurance product: a licensed surety company underwrites the risk that a defendant fails to appear, and we act as the licensed agent who posts the bond and manages the relationship with your family. If forfeiture happens, the surety company covers the bond amount — which is precisely why the underwriting (your ID, address, income, and any collateral) matters to us upfront.</p>
      <p>This is different from paying cash bail directly to the court, and different from an unsecured promise with no company standing behind it. The surety structure is what lets a family post a $10,000 bond for a premium in the hundreds or low thousands, rather than needing $10,000 in cash on hand.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="glass-card reveal">
